dashboard/node_modules/

# Results and artifacts (regenerate with `robot-ci experiment run`)
experiments/results/*
!experiments/results/.gitkeep

# Recorded experiment video, images and ZIP packages.
#
# These are the only generated files in the project that are large *and*
# unregenerable-by-inspection: an MP4 of an episode is tens of megabytes and a
# reviewer gains nothing from it being in git history, because
# `scripts/record_suite.py` rebuilds it from the seed and the manifest. The
# manifests, summaries and READMEs are small and are the part worth keeping, so
# those stay tracked and the media does not.
artifacts/visual_reports/*/
artifacts/visual_reports/*.zip
artifacts/visual_reports/*.mp4
!artifacts/visual_reports/suite_summary.json
!artifacts/visual_reports/SUITE.md

# ...with one deliberate exception: the evidence behind the frozen baseline.
#
# Results are ignorable only as long as something else can regenerate them. A
# research baseline is a different thing -- it is a claim that a specific set of
# measurements was made at a specific commit, and that claim is only checkable if
# the measurements are in the tag. Committing the artifact is the same discipline
# as committing the test count: a result nobody can inspect is not a result.
#
# The large per-episode directories (demo_v1_vs_v3/, phase3_pairing/) stay out on
# size alone; their summaries and the verification record are kept.
experiments/results/*
!experiments/results/*.json
!experiments/results/*.txt
!experiments/results/*.md
!experiments/results/*.png
!experiments/results/.gitkeep
# The measured-results record is source, not a generated artifact. It is the
# only thing in this directory that is hand-written, and it is the file that
# keeps a placeholder from being mistaken for a measurement later on.
!experiments/results/README.md
!experiments/results/DEMO.md
*.jsonl
*.sqlite
*.db

